  "appendix": {
    "methodology": "Assets are ingested from CycloneDX 1.6 CBOMs and any manual register, deduplicated by a deterministic identity, linked to business systems and data classes from the context file, classified for quantum vulnerability using the rule pack, and scored. The Mosca inequality (X + Y > Z) compares how long data must stay secret (X, confidentiality lifetime) plus the time to migrate (Y) against the years until a cryptographically relevant quantum computer (Z), per user-supplied scenario. Harvest-now-decrypt-later (HNDL) marks Shor-broken key establishment or encryption over data that outlives Z.",
    "scoring_formula": "final = (0.40*quantum_vulnerability + 0.30*mosca_exposure + 0.20*criticality + 0.10*evidence_confidence) / sum_of_weights; all terms in [0,1]",
    "weights": {
      "quantum_vulnerability": 0.4,
      "mosca_exposure": 0.3,
      "criticality": 0.2,
      "evidence_confidence": 0.1
    },
